% SCAFFOLDING stand-in for SIMPOS's class `post_queue_for_message`,
% compiled by psi/espc.py into the package `simpos`.  It is NOT SIMPOS:
% no part of it is printed.  It is INTERPOLATED (labelled) from TM-100
% section 3.2 (2)(a) (PDF p15, docs/simpos/printed/listings/
% tm0100_p15.esp): the printed channel's slot initialiser creates it,
% and "all the predicates of class 'post_queue_for_message' which are
% called by a channel must be compatible to those of class 'post_queue'
% called by a stream".
% Model (OURS): it inherits the INTERPOLATED post_queue stand-in
% (post_queue.esp) unchanged, so add_object/2 and remove_object/2 are
% post_queue's.  The "more efficient" message handling TM-100 mentions
% is not modelled.

class post_queue_for_message has

% INTERPOLATED from: TM-100 p15 (compatible with post_queue; see above).
nature post_queue;

% INTERPOLATED from: the printed channel slot initialiser
% `( post_queue := Queue :- :create(#post_queue_for_message, Queue) )`
% (TM-100 Fig. 3.7, PDF p15), the same shape as post_queue's create/2.
:create(Class, Queue) :- :new(Class, Queue);

end.
